WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
Tesla started Earthworks on a 3,000 acre Texas site for a $10 billion solar factory projected

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:13.300
to create 9,712 permanent jobs. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 661. First principles,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:19.000
electric semis on daily routes, and a glass roof redesign follow. Fort Bend County, Tesla

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Roddy reports, is where Tesla's project Crystal Sun is now being graded on that same track.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.620
Flyover drone footage from Estice, Robinson, Jr. released this morning shows large

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.560
clearings, equipment staging areas, and existing homesteads still in use, and

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.800
active leveling across a substantial portion of the property. The plant is

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.060
designed to make the full solar chain from silicon ingots and wafers to coated

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:48.173
cells and finished modules. Operations are targeted for the first quarter of

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:55.193
2029. Construction itself is targeted for 2026 through 2028. Tesla projects the permanent

00:00:55.193 --> 00:01:02.513
workforce will ramp from roughly 1,900 positions in the first year of operations to that 9,712

00:01:02.513 --> 00:01:08.913
figure by 2033, with a peak of about 1,147 construction jobs during the build.

00:01:09.876 --> 00:01:14.956
Public filings first submitted in July under Texas's Jobs, Energy, Technology and Innovation

00:01:14.956 --> 00:01:18.836
Act, described that full chain from ingots to finished modules.

00:01:19.516 --> 00:01:24.216
Lamar consolidated independent school district unanimously approved school tax limitations

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:24.916
in September.

00:01:25.676 --> 00:01:29.556
Fort Bend County commissioners approved a package of abatements and related agreements

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:34.576
in late October that could extend equipment tax breaks for as long as 35 years.

00:01:35.216 --> 00:01:39.516
Tesla had previously indicated it was evaluating a competing out-of-state location.

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:45.036
Elon Musk has said Tesla and SpaceX are each working toward 100 gigawatts of annual

00:01:45.036 --> 00:01:47.196
US solar manufacturing capacity.

00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:52.316
And if built as described, Project Crystal Sun would stand as one of the largest domestic

00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:56.296
attempts to create a fully integrated solar supply chain on American soil.

00:01:57.215 --> 00:02:01.595
Building that entire chain on one site is a bet against the fragmented model the rest

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:02.955
of the industry still uses.

00:02:03.335 --> 00:02:07.995
Capital has to be committed years ahead of revenue if Tesla wants control over every

00:02:07.995 --> 00:02:10.155
step that sets panel cost and quality.

00:02:10.835 --> 00:02:16.495
An accompanying economic analysis estimates the project could add roughly $107 billion to

00:02:16.495 --> 00:02:20.555
Texas gross domestic product, or GDP, over several decades.

00:02:21.135 --> 00:02:25.395
That figure rests on vertical integration, cutting exposure to imported wafers and

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:28.535
cells whose prices have swung sharply in recent years.

00:02:29.035 --> 00:02:34.035
By owning the conversion from raw silicon to finished modules, Tesla can adjust output

00:02:34.035 --> 00:02:39.535
mix and process parameters without renegotiating supplier contracts or waiting on third-party

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:40.875
capacity expansions.

00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:45.895
The same logic that once justified building its own battery lines now applies to solar,

00:02:46.315 --> 00:02:49.775
where module margins have compressed as Chinese production scaled.

00:02:50.415 --> 00:02:55.215
For customers and utilities, the practical result is a more predictable supply of domestically

00:02:55.215 --> 00:02:57.295
produced panels paired with storage.

00:02:57.975 --> 00:03:02.455
When the factory reaches the planned scale, it removes one layer of price volatility that

00:03:02.455 --> 00:03:05.335
has slowed solar plus storage adoption in some markets.

00:03:05.975 --> 00:03:10.315
Those already approved 35-year equipment tax abatement's further lower the effective

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:15.215
capital cost, shifting the break even point earlier than a non-integrated competitor

00:03:15.215 --> 00:03:16.715
could achieve on the same site.

00:03:17.275 --> 00:03:21.875
The bet is that control over the entire process will matter more than speed to first panel,

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:24.555
and more than any single supplier relationship.

00:03:25.658 --> 00:03:31.038
Electric semi-trucks, electric reports, are covering over 600 miles every day in real-world

00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:31.638
operation.

00:03:31.638 --> 00:03:36.678
Those distances are being logged by fleets already in service, not in a lab cycle.

00:03:37.358 --> 00:03:42.098
Model Y owners, auto blog reports, are still frustrated with the automatic Wiper system.

00:03:42.718 --> 00:03:47.258
The complaints are ongoing and tied to daily usability, not a one-week software glitch.

00:03:48.295 --> 00:03:53.875
Franz von Holzhausen told Jay Leno, Tesla Roddy notes, that usage data showed owners open

00:03:53.875 --> 00:03:57.075
the sunroof when they first got the car, then rarely after.

00:03:57.655 --> 00:04:01.055
The mechanism was complex, heavy, and often required service.

00:04:01.675 --> 00:04:05.955
Tessla's shifted development to heat and UV reflecting laminated glass instead.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.140
Tessla's all-glass roofs pass the same federal roof-crush test as metal roofs.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.860
The Model 3 glass roof held about four times the car's own weight in that test, well over

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.500
the federal minimum of three times.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.760
In 2013, the Model S roof broke the testing machine at more than four times its weight

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.700
before giving way.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.700
Zero fatalities have occurred in any crashes involving these roofs.

